        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e5406d3c-32ab-5eb4-b80d-90a2f97b91d5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Midnight Oil, Switchfoot\n- People: Peter Garrett, Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, Drew Shirley\n- Songs: \"Beds Are Burning\"\n- Albums: \"Diesel and Dust\"\n- Places: Sydney, San Diego, California\n- Topics: band formation, membership\n\nFacts:\n- By late 1976, Peter Garrett moved to Sydney to complete his law degree.\n- By late 1976, the band Farm changed its name to Midnight Oil by drawing the name from a hat.\n- \"Beds Are Burning\" is a 1987 song by the Australian rock band Midnight Oil.\n- \"Beds Are Burning\" is the first track on Midnight Oil's album \"Diesel and Dust\".\n- Switchfoot is an American alternative rock band from San Diego, California.\n- Switchfoot's members are Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, and Drew Shirley.\n- Jon Foreman performs lead vocals and guitar in Switchfoot.\n- Tim Foreman performs bass guitar and backing vocals in Switchfoot.\n- Chad Butler performs drums and percussion in Switchfoot.\n- Jerome Fontamillas performs guitar, keyboards, and backing vocals in Switchfoot.\n- Drew Shirley performs guitar and backing vocals in Switchfoot.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
